<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Black Loyalists</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Black Loyalists were people of African descent, many formerly enslaved, who sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a> in return for promises of freedom. About 3,000 were evacuated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a> in 1783, settling at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/birchtown">Birchtown</a> and elsewhere, but faced poor land and discrimination. In 1792 about 1,100 of them sailed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a> and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freetown">Freetown</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/black-loyalists.jpg" alt="Black Loyalists" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Di (they-them) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Black_Loyalist_Heritage_Society_coat_of_arms.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
